// The integration scenario, as a library.
//
// It used to be the body of ext/cmd/integration's `main`, which meant the only
// way to run it was against a real workspace with a real token -- so the checks
// it makes (does the encoder agree with the parser, does a block payload
// round-trip, does a bad channel refuse the way we think) ran when somebody
// remembered, and never in CI.
//
// Split out here, `run` takes a `Client` and does not care what is behind it:
// ext/cmd/integration still points it at Slack, and ext/test/mockrun points it
// at marianoguerra/slack/mock, in CI, on every commit. Two runs of one
// scenario is the whole design -- the mock's fidelity is then defined by
// something other than the mock's own tests.
//
// This package must NOT import marianoguerra/slack/mock. `run` takes a client;
// the caller supplies the transport. That is what keeps ext/cmd/integration a
// pure real-Slack binary.
import {
  "marianoguerra/slack/api",
  "marianoguerra/slack/blocks",
  "marianoguerra/slack/client",
  "marianoguerra/slack/methods",
  "moonbitlang/core/json",
}

supported_targets = "+native"
